gnome-remote-desktop (50.1+rkmpp+git20260717.2571326-0ubuntu1~exp3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Use FFmpeg's existing AV_CODEC_FLAG_LOW_DELAY contract with the matching
    hardened FFmpeg package, which bounds synchronous RKMPP waits internally.
    No GRD-specific FFmpeg API or private option is introduced.
  * Reuse a validated RKMPP context after the smoke test and on stale-frame
    refreshes. Force an IDR and refresh the whole frame without repeatedly
    destroying and reopening MPP.
  * Treat a timed-out AVC hardware encode as recoverable: release the failed
    frame, reset the render context, use software encoding for a cooldown, and
    retry hardware later instead of failing the graphics subsystem.
  * Move pipeline diagnostics to an independent main context/thread so the
    starvation warning remains live if the RDP graphics thread blocks.

