gnome-remote-desktop (50.1+rkmpp-2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Revert "rdp: make handover reconnect cleanup robust" (4e0d599): it broke the
    basic GDM->session handover (stall, refcount underflow, zombie remote
    displays from its preserve-on-failure path). Back to stock 50.1 handover.
  * encode-session-ffmpeg: make mainline FFmpeg's h264_rkmpp produce a usable
    AVC420 stream. Mainline's rkmpp encoder (unlike the ffmpeg-rockchip fork)
    exposes no QP/profile knobs and ignores per-frame forced IDR, so it needs two
    mainline-specific workarounds (both no-ops on the fork):
    - Recreate the encoder after the start-up smoke encode so the first client
      frame is a real IDR (SPS+PPS+IDR). rkmpp only emits an IDR for the first
      frame after open and the smoke encode consumed it; mainline ignores
      pict_type=I, so every frame went out as a bare P-slice, the client never
      decoded or acknowledged a frame, and the RDPGFX frame controller froze the
      surface after two unacknowledged frames.
    - Set the VBR peak/floor (rc_max_rate/rc_min_rate) and raise the target.
      Mainline only sets MPP bps_max from avctx->rc_max_rate, which was unset, so
      MPP's ~2.5 Mbps default ceiling capped every frame; with no QP knob on
      mainline, a higher target is what keeps QP low. Fixes heavy artifacts.

 -- Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>  Tue, 30 Jun 2026 21:15:00 -0700

